=== PRE-REGISTRATION (diagnosis) 13:20 -- where does the 07 split enter?
Instrument: determinism_arm.py now gives each run its own ZBENCH_DUMP_REQUESTS subdir (run-k), so runs can be diffed
call by call with bench/results/_diffcalls.py, which classifies the FIRST difference as a dump-only field, a
server-minted id, or real content.
  D1  07-ttl-cache, 27b, real-user cell + fix, temp 0, N=3, dumps on, zc-01.
  D2  07-ttl-cache, 35b (zds-qwen3.6-35b), same cell, N=3, dumps on, zc-01 -- the task-vs-model control.
Reading the first content difference between any two diverging runs:
  (i)  the first differing call differs in its INPUT (a tool result -- e.g. a pytest timing line or a listing order)
       while every earlier call is identical -> the split enters through the ENVIRONMENT; the loop is deterministic
       given its inputs; remedy candidates are at the tool-output layer (normalising volatile fields), pre-registered
       separately before any is shipped.
  (ii) the first differing call has IDENTICAL input and a different assistant message follows -> the split is the
       PROVIDER's (the 27b under long agentic prompts), despite P0's 5/5 on fixed prompts; the 35b control decides
       whether it is model-specific.
  (iii) no split reproduces in D1 (3/3 identical) -> the earlier split was a low-rate event; report the rate over
       all 6 runs, no attribution.
Predictions: D1 splits at least once (2 of 3 already did); D2 -- not predicted (never measured on 07).
The 35b's 3/3 on 06/07/08 in ADR-0156 measured capability, not bytes.

